NAME: constants defined by expressions
DESCRIPTION: pMARS substitutes an EQU's text before evaluating, so a constant's value must keep its own parentheses: a = 1+2 used as a*3 is 9, not 7; see behtests/const_expressions.beh
SRC:
(program
  (const a (+ 1 2))
  (const b (* a 3))
  (const n -5)
  (const m (- 0 n))
  (seq
    (JMP 0)
    (DAT (* a 3) b)
    (DAT (- 10 a) (- 0 a))
    (DAT 0 (- 1 m))))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b
a EQU (1+2)
b EQU (a*3)
n EQU (-5)
m EQU (0-n)

  JMP    #0     , #0     
  DAT    #a*3   , #b     
  DAT    #10-a  , #0-a   
  DAT    #0     , #1-m   
  DAT    $0     , $0     